Here's a minimal API endpoint that accepts multiple image files plus a text description via `multipart/form-data`:

```csharp
// Program.cs

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Raise the max request body size to 50 MB (default is ~28 MB)
builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(o => o.Limits.MaxRequestBodySize = 50 * 1024 * 1024);

var app = builder.Build();

app.MapPost("/upload", async (
    IFormFileCollection files,
    [FromForm] string description,
    CancellationToken ct) =>
{
    // Validate that we actually received images
    string[] allowed = [".jpg", ".jpeg", ".png", ".gif", ".webp"];

    foreach (var file in files)
    {
        var ext = Path.GetExtension(file.FileName).ToLowerInvariant();
        if (!allowed.Contains(ext))
            return Results.BadRequest($"File '{file.FileName}' is not an allowed image type.");
    }

    var uploadDir = Path.Combine(app.Environment.ContentRootPath, "uploads");
    Directory.CreateDirectory(uploadDir);

    var saved = new List<string>();

    foreach (var file in files)
    {
        // Prefix with a GUID to avoid name collisions
        var safeName = $"{Guid.NewGuid():N}_{Path.GetFileName(file.FileName)}";
        var dest = Path.Combine(uploadDir, safeName);

        await using var stream = File.Create(dest);
        await file.CopyToAsync(stream, ct);
        saved.Add(safeName);
    }

    return Results.Ok(new
    {
        description,
        fileCount = saved.Count,
        fileNames = saved
    });
})
.DisableAntiforgery();          // required for minimal-API form binding without AF token

app.Run();
```

**Key points:**

- **`IFormFileCollection`** binds all files from the form regardless of field name. Use `[FromForm] IFormFile file` for a single file.
- **`[FromForm] string description`** binds the text field named `description` from the same multipart form.
- **`ConfigureKestrel`** raises the body size limit to 50 MB. If you're behind a reverse proxy (NGINX, IIS), raise its limit too.
- **`.DisableAntiforgery()`** is needed because minimal APIs enforce antiforgery on form endpoints by default in .NET 8.

**Example `curl` call:**

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/upload \
  -F "description=My vacation photos" \
  -F "files=@photo1.jpg" \
  -F "files=@photo2.png"
```
